{"name":"Tungsten","hex":"#b5ac9f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tungsten","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rare metallic chemical element (symbol W, from Latin wolframium) with an atomic number of 74.","Any of various commercially available alloys principally of tungsten."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tungsten"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tungsten","blocks":[{"text":"Tungsten is a chemical element; it has symbol W and atomic number 74. It is a metal found naturally on Earth almost exclusively in compounds with other elements. It was identified as a distinct element in 1781 and first isolated as a metal in 1783. Its important ores include scheelite and wolframite, the latter lending the element its alternative name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Wolfram_evaporated_crystals_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Wolfram_evaporated_crystals_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tungsten"},{"title":"Tungsten (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Tungsten is a Swedish power metal band formed by ex-HammerFall drummer Anders Johansson and his two sons."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Tungsten_%28band%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tungsten_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Tungsten_rod_with_oxidised_surface.jpg/330px-Tungsten_rod_with_oxidised_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Tungsten_rod_with_oxidised_surface.jpg/330px-Tungsten_rod_with_oxidised_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tungsten rod with oxidised surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATungsten_rod_wit